      "writtenOn": "2022-01-13T23:12:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like a more concrete example of the use case.\n\nWe should avoid extending/changing the legacy cros-ec interface.  Can the new code just call gpio_pin_configure() in the Zephyr API directly?\n\nIf this is done by a driver or board code during some init, I don\u0027t know that it\u0027s worth tracking whether gpio_pin_configure() has already been called.  If there are possible side effects to calling gpio_pin_configure() twice, then we should enhance the upstream GPIO API to add a gpio_pin_get_config().  This function would return an error if the pin has not been configured.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 342,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "26e83271378780c05c4941baae45924678b897b1",
