      "writtenOn": "2022-01-14T19:38:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m good with the last option.  The named-gpios provides a property that informs init_gpios() to skip the gpio_pin_configure() step.  When the board code decides that it really does need the GPIO, it can call gpio_pin_configure() directly.\n\nI\u0027m inclined to not use the \"status\" property for this check.  It seems like the Zephyr convention is that if \"status \u003d disabled\", then the entire node is skipped and is not available to the C code.  So I\u0027d like to see this managed with a separate bool property.",
